From cf631abc6d001d65a993e790ed63e7847b38c00e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:49:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve echo binding uncertainty across output sink
 checks

A locally shadowed echo can evaluate its quoted argument. Revoke the parentheses exemption on functions, binding-changing commands, escapes and dynamic parameter words, and retain the raw source through secondary masking. Ordinary literal revision echoes remain allowed. The optional parameter-prefix allowance is deliberately withdrawn.

Proof: 74 focused tests green before one additional passing heredoc-context test; 18 generated real Bash marker cases exercise function, alias, source and computed-loader bindings. Public oversized-script regressions remain refused. Full final-head cron suite and independent review pending.
